From 6ae5e5876ead9349857e9a50e3fdc7156f4b96c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BrLumen <igflocal@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:06:32 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Session: close the device when the session is destroyed

Commit 4d6c6ea3 ("Fix #605 by closing current device when another is
selected") made Session::set_device() close the previous device, but a
session that is destroyed (its tab closed, or PulseView quitting) still
leaves its device open: DeviceManager keeps every HardwareDevice alive in
its device list (and in user_spec_device_ for -d), so the device object
is never destructed and its close() never runs.

For USB devices this goes unnoticed. Serial drivers hold their port
exclusively while the device is open, so after closing a session tab
every later scan fails with "Resource busy" and the device cannot be
used again until PulseView is restarted.

Close the device in the Session destructor, mirroring set_device().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: BrLumen <igflocal@gmail.com>
---
 pv/session.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pv/session.cpp b/pv/session.cpp
index 03770097..cf0ee5c6 100644
--- a/pv/session.cpp
+++ b/pv/session.cpp
@@ -137,6 +137,13 @@ Session::~Session()
 	// Stop and join to the thread
 	stop_capture();
 
+	// Release the device. The DeviceManager keeps the device object alive,
+	// so it would otherwise stay open after the session is gone; serial
+	// drivers hold their port exclusively while open, which blocks every
+	// later scan and session from using the device.
+	if (device_)
+		device_->close();
+
 	for (SignalGroup* group : signal_groups_) {
 		group->clear();
 		delete group;
-- 
